### One-click launch

Don't want to type a command? Double-click **`{{ launch_name }}.bat`** (Windows)
or run **`./"{{ launch_name }}.sh"`** (macOS / Linux). It uses `uv` if present
(auto-syncing deps on first run), otherwise the installed `{{ project_slug }}`
command, and {% if interfaces.web %}starts the web UI, opening it in your browser{% else %}starts an interactive chat in the terminal{% endif %}.
Nothing installed yet? On a fresh machine the launcher offers to install `uv`
for you (user-level, no admin — uv brings its own Python), then continues; the
first run needs network to fetch uv + dependencies, later runs are local.
Behind a corporate proxy the launcher reuses your **system proxy** (Windows
registry / macOS Settings) for that first `uv sync` — no need to export anything,
and its PyPI reachability probe goes through the same proxy so it won't wrongly
fall back to a mirror the proxy can't reach. If official PyPI is slow through your
proxy, pin a faster one for the run: `UV_DEFAULT_INDEX=<mirror-url>`.

