## MCP tools (capability baseline)

Beyond a couple of safe built-ins (a `write_todos` planning scratchpad, a clock,
a calculator), this harness has no built-in **capability** tools (file / shell /
web) — those come from [MCP](https://modelcontextprotocol.io) servers, prefilled
in `config.yaml`:
web **search** (`web-search`, keyless, multi-engine with failover), **`fetch`** (read a URL), and **`git`**
read tools are on; mutating `git` and **Desktop Commander** (terminal + files)
are predefined but off (the agent will ask you to enable one when a task needs
it). uvx servers are prewarmed and baked into the Docker image so `docker run`
works offline. Add more with `harnessmith new --mcp-server <name>` or by pasting
a marketplace block into `config.yaml`. Allowlist tools as `<server>__<tool>`;
read-only tools (`safe_tools`) are also offered to `plan`/`ask`. Secrets are
referenced by env-var name only — a remote server's bearer token (`auth_env`) and
a stdio server's injected vars (`env`) are seeded into `.env.example` by name; fill
their **values**{% if interfaces.web %} from the **MCP** tab's per-server **Auth** section (write-only to `.env`, never echoed — same as the LLM key box) or{% endif %} by editing `.env`.

**First run / connectivity.** The very first `serve`/`chat` pre-fetches each
`uvx`/`npx` server's package once, printing live progress (with a heartbeat so a
slow download never looks frozen) in the terminal you launched from; a marker
(`.harness/.mcp-warmed`) records it, so every later launch skips straight to a fast
cache hit. By the time the page opens, tools are ready. (The one-shot `run` skips
this — it's the scripting/Docker path.) Connecting is two-phase: the package is
pre-fetched in a survivable step (so a slow download finishes once and isn't killed
by the handshake timeout), then the session handshake runs. If a connect fails, it
**heals on its own** — retrying in the background with backoff (`connect_max_retries`):
the web **MCP** tab shows it **connecting** (amber) while retrying and **red** only
once retries are exhausted, and tools light up by themselves once it recovers. (A
missing launcher — no **Node**/**uv** — goes red right away; retrying can't conjure
it.) Each server also has a **Reconnect** button (retry just that one). Adding a server from
the **MCP** tab enables its whole toolset by default (narrow it on the Tools tab).
When PyPI
or the npm registry is unreachable, `uvx`/`npx` are pointed at a domestic mirror
automatically (only if you haven't set your own index). Node servers (web-search,
Desktop Commander) need **Node.js**; since Windows rarely ships it, the one-click launcher offers
to fetch a **portable Node** into your user folder (no admin, not committed to the
repo) and adds it to PATH for that run — a missing Node is otherwise reported with
an install hint. See [`AGENTS.md`](./AGENTS.md).
{% endif %}{% if spec.skills.enabled %}
## Skills

Supports the open [Agent Skills](https://modelcontextprotocol.io) standard
(`SKILL.md`). Each skill's name + description is injected into the system prompt;
the model loads the full instructions on demand with the `read_skill` tool. Drop
a folder under `skills/<name>/SKILL.md` to add one (see `config.yaml` →
`skills.dirs`). Any skills you selected at generation time are already under
`skills/`. See [`AGENTS.md`](./AGENTS.md).
