## Long-term memory (cross-session)

The agent keeps a small, self-maintained note that persists **across sessions**
(durable facts, your preferences, decisions), injected into every system prompt.
It writes it itself with the `memory_append` / `memory_write` tools and reads it
with `memory_read`. The built-in `file` backend is one human-readable markdown
note (`.harness/memory.md`, gitignored, **never holds secrets**):

```bash
{{ project_slug }} memory show         # print the note
{{ project_slug }} memory path         # print the note's file path
{{ project_slug }} memory clear        # forget everything
{{ project_slug }} memory consolidate  # condense it (compaction model) when it grows large
```

It's a few notes the agent curates on purpose — distinct from RAG. Only
`inject_max_chars` of the note is injected, so when it outgrows that, consolidate
it (manually above, or set `auto_consolidate: true` to do it at chat-session end).
Tune it under `memory:` in `config.yaml`{% if interfaces.web %} or the web **Memory** config tab (backend,
capacity, read-only, a memory *policy*, and the note itself){% endif %}, or plug in your own
backend (vector DB, mem0, …) with `@register_memory` — see [`AGENTS.md`](./AGENTS.md).
{% endif %}{% if spec.subagents.enabled %}
## Multi-agent (subagents)

This agent can **delegate** independent subtasks to specialized worker subagents —
the orchestrator-worker / agent-as-tool pattern. There's no new mode to pick: the
agent itself calls a `subagents` tool when it judges delegation is worth it, and
lists **several** subtasks in one call to run them in **parallel**. Each worker
runs in its own fresh context with its own tools and model, then returns a result
the main agent synthesizes.

Configure the roster under `subagents:` in `config.yaml` (each worker's name,
prompt, `role` = which LLM profile, its own `tools` allowlist, and `max_steps`).
Workers never get the `subagents` tool, so the topology is fixed at depth 1 (no
runaway recursion). It's plain code over a thread pool — no agent framework. See
[`AGENTS.md`](./AGENTS.md).
{% endif %}
## Layout

```
config.yaml                 # runtime config (non-secret); only env-var NAMES
.env.example                # copy to .env and fill in real secret values
harness.spec.yaml           # snapshot of the spec this repo was generated from
src/{{ project_slug }}/
  harness/
    config.py               # load config.yaml + .env, validate
    llm.py                  # OpenAI Chat Completions client (+ provider-neutral types)
    llm_anthropic.py        # native Anthropic Messages client (provider: anthropic profiles)
    loop.py                 # thin dispatcher: pick a paradigm by mode and run it
    paradigms/              # the function-calling loops you own (read these first)
      __init__.py           #   paradigm registry + shared RunResult/plumbing
      agent.py              #   agent (default; ReAct-style tool-calling loop){% for p in paradigms %}{% if p == "plan" %}
      plan.py               #   read-only planning{% elif p == "ask" %}
      ask.py                #   read-only Q&A{% endif %}{% endfor %}
    tools.py                # tool registry + built-in safe tools
    hooks.py                # lifecycle hooks (extend without touching the loop)
    trace.py                # JSONL trace + token/cost accounting
    debuglog.py             # opt-in local debug log (names/counts only — never content)
    session.py              # save/resume a conversation (.harness/sessions/<id>.json)
    prompts.py              # system-prompt assembly
    mock.py                 # offline MockLLM for tests / --mock
{% if spec.mcp.enabled %}    mcp.py                  # optional MCP tool bridge (stdio + remote)
{% endif %}{% if spec.skills.enabled %}    skills.py               # standard Agent Skills (SKILL.md discovery + read_skill)
{% endif %}{% if spec.memory.enabled %}    memory.py               # cross-session long-term memory (@register_memory + file backend)
{% endif %}{% if spec.subagents.enabled %}    subagents.py            # multi-agent: subagents tool delegates to scoped worker subagents (parallel)
{% endif %}  interfaces/
    cli.py                  # `run` (one turn, resumable) + `chat` (multi-turn REPL)
{% if interfaces.web %}    web.py                  # `serve` — FastAPI SSE chat + live /config panel
{% endif %}tests/                      # mock-driven tests (no API key needed)
```

## Configuration

`config.yaml` holds everything non-secret (models, roles, prompts, enabled
tools, per-LLM pricing + cost limits, tracing). Secrets are referenced by
**env-var name** only; the
real values live in `.env` (gitignored) or the process environment — they never
touch git, the trace, or `harness.spec.yaml`.

**Always-apply project rules:** list markdown files under `prompts.rules_files`
and their text is injected into every system prompt — the open `AGENTS.md` /
`CLAUDE.md` / `.cursor/rules` pattern.{% if "RULES.md" in spec.prompts.rules_files %} A starter `RULES.md` ships here; edit
it freely.{% endif %} A `CLAUDE.md` at the project root is auto-injected even if
unlisted; `AGENTS.md` is **not** (it's this harness's dev guide, not a runtime
rule). See [`AGENTS.md`](./AGENTS.md).

